WEBVTT

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.860
Hey, wasn't that...

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.400
Sophie...

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.490
...chan... or not.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.580
<i>A blonde girl?</i>

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.340
Did you just say "Sophie"?

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.410
She's a girl about this tall 
with long silver hair.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.510
I heard a rumor that someone saw her here.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.270
Are you a friend of hers?

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.150
Yes.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.980
We've been friends for a long time.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.400
Are you, by chance, a vampire?

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.910
That's right. Seems I don't need to explain it.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.410
I just arrived from America to visit Sophie.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.530
Wow, it's so nice to meet you!

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.500
My name is Amano Akari.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.910
I'm living with Sophie-chan.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:58.880
With her?

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.950
Oh, I see.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.480
What's your name?

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:08.950
I'm Ellie.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:43.510
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:43.510
<b>Sophie and Ellie</b>

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.660
Is it okay if I come in?

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.800
Of course! Come in!

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.500
Thank you for having me.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:04.360
<i>She looks like a cute little doll!</i>

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:07.470
<i>She's got a different feel to 
her than Sophie-chan, though.</i>

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.890
Should I go wake Sophie-chan?

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.190
I think she'll wake up soon. I'll just wait.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:21.510
Are you hungry at all?

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.340
Want some sweets? 
I have strawberry daifuku.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.910
Oh, thank you. You're very kind.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.480
Oh, right... You're a vampire.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.500
Want to drink some blood, then?

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.550
We've got all different types in the fridge.

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.410
Wow, you're quite considerate.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.570
I've got the perfect dress 
here! Want to put it on?

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.150
How about trying on this ribbon?

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.850
I-I'll pass.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.380
Oh, you're awake!

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.080
Good morning.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.810
Sophie! I've missed you so much!

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.150
It's been, like, a hundred years!

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.450
Ellie? How did you know I was here?

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:01.080
I hired someone to help me find you!

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:03.020
Such a touching moment!

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.800
I'm so happy for you, Sophie-chan.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.770
Akari, why'd you let her in here?

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:13.050
Wait, you're not happy to 
see your long-time friend?

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.520
I wouldn't call her a friend.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:18.410
You wouldn't?

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:19.530
That's right.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.740
She and I aren't friends.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.690
We're lovers.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:27.660
Stop saying random nonsense.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.830
We're just acquaintances.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.410
Aw, I made you blush. That's so cute.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.120
<i>Could it be that Sophie-chan 
can't really deal with her?</i>

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:38.940
With Ellie being so whimsical, I've 
always suffered collateral damage.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.850
Seeing her after all this time brings 
back a lot of traumatic memories.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.590
We're going to go see the public execution!

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:50.030
I don't want to see it...

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.310
We're moving to the new continent!

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.740
I'm so seasick.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:02.440
Hey! That wasn't trauma.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.290
Those were wonderful memories.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:05.880
Anyway...

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.330
Seeing you two side by side makes it seem 
like Sophie-chan gained a little sister!

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.250
I'm the older one here!

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.650
I'm over 450 years old!

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:18.210
I'm almost 100 years younger than her!

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.210
Whoops.

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:24.520
Ellie-chan, you must be exhausted 
after your long journey.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:27.460
Would you like to take a bath?
I just filled the tub.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.310
Really? Thank you.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.780
I'll do that.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.990
I'm only coming in here to bring more shampoo.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.430
Not because I have indecent motives.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.240
Ellie-chan, I brought some new shampoo...

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:09.770
Is something wrong?

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:13.230
The water is completely red!

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.180
Oh, Sophie!

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:19.770
I helped myself to the blood in the fridge...

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:20.900
as a bath additive.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:25.400
A blood bath just makes your skin so silky.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.220
You used all of it, didn't you?

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.860
That stuff is expensive. Don't waste it.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.020
That scared me!

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.290
I'm glad she's not hurt or anything.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:45.170
Hey, Sophie, I'm hungry.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:48.590
Well, you poured all the 
blood into the bathtub.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:54.830
I'd much rather drink your fresh 
blood than that bottled stuff.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:55.890
Stop it.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.850
What's wrong? Am I embarrassing you?

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.820
No, your fangs hurt.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.490
Whoa! Ellie-chan, stop!

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.560
Akari! You saved me.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.730
Are you trying to get in my way?

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:13.330
I'll go get a camera!

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:13.330
Hey!

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.300
Looks like we're alone again.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.250
Well, then, I'll just dig in.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.190
Akari!

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:26.860
That was good.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.000
What, it's already over?

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.900
I was hoping to get a romantic picture...

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:38.010
Maybe I'll try you next, while I'm at it.

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:42.240
A young girl's blood is the best.

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:44.590
Akari's blood is gross.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.890
I won't know until I try it.

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:49.410
You smell good.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:50.650
Um...

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:54.840
It's so bad, you'll be 
traumatized after just one sip.

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:57.480
I-It's that bad?

00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:58.930
I guess I'll pass, then.

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:02.610
My blood tastes that bad?!

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.090
I'm kind of shocked!

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:10.090
Sheesh, Ellie. You immediately 
want to bite people.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:14.790
Nowadays, putting your fangs into 
someone's neck to feed is so passé.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:16.000
It is?

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.970
What's this? Are you jealous?

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.320
That I got close to another girl?

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:22.680
You couldn't be more wrong.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:28.230
Don't worry. You know you're 
my favorite girl in the world.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.560
Gee, thanks.

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:32.190
Hey, how dare you wipe my love away?!

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:39.030
Why is Sophie always so cold to me?

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:41.780
I remember her being nicer before...

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.660
Or maybe not...

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:46.060
Have I wronged you somehow?

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:48.530
Just today, you completely 
emptied my fridge,

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:51.230
and then you forcibly sucked my blood.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.540
Then you tried to go after Akari.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:55.700
Now, now...

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:58.070
Also, don't touch my figures.

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:00.020
Whoops, it broke.

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:03.810
You... will regret that!

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.010
Now, now...

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:08.490
<b>Super Glue</b>

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.490
If I start yelling at you, it'll never end.

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:10.920
I'll just consider it a 
natural disaster and give up.

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:13.870
Anyway, I haven't seen you in so long.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:15.800
What have you been up to all this time?

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.920
Did something happen?

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:24.450
One day, I was so tired from 
playing that I fell asleep.

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:36.000
When I woke up...

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.140
Oh, no... It's morning.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.670
Looks like I slept far too late.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:45.480
When I looked outside, the scenery 
looked completely different.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:48.190
Oh, my.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:50.780
I looked at the date and saw 
that a hundred years had passed.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.820
So because of that, nothing happened.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.650
You were asleep the whole time?

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:02.110
<i>When vampires oversleep, 
it's on a totally different scale!</i>

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:03.990
Wait, I get why you're so cold to me!

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:08.590
You're upset that I didn't come 
visit you in a hundred years.

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:09.600
What?

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:13.290
This is the longest we've ever 
gone without seeing each other.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:17.500
I never told you my address because
I was always the one who visited you.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.640
I'm right, aren't I?

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:23.170
You're so badly behaved,
I was sure a vampire hunter

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:25.220
had gotten you by now.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:29.590
Oh, you were worried I was dead?

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:33.250
I'm really sorry.

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:35.840
But you're the very first 
person I came to visit

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.630
once I woke up, so don't be mad.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:40.040
I'm not mad or anything.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:43.530
But... I'm glad nothing bad happened to you.

00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:48.160
<i>It looks like they really 
are friends after all.</i>

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:49.490
<i>I'm glad.</i>

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:50.670
I know!

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.500
I'll give you a kiss to seal 
our renewed friendship!

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:55.130
This time, on the lips!

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:56.990
I think not.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:59.470
<i>They are friends, right?</i>

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:05.560
I need to get to bed.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.220
I stayed up so late.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:08.210
Right.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:10.400
Not getting enough sleep 
is bad for your skin.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.640
Goodnight!

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:12.450
Night.

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:16.500
And what have you been up to lately?

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:19.280
I'm sure a lot happened in 
the last hundred years.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:20.620
I guess.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.860
I watched movies, played video games...

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:25.100
And lately, I've been on the internet.

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:28.610
Oh, that reminds me. I need to go 
for a walk before the night's over.

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:29.830
A walk?

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:33.330
Apparently walks are good for your 
health and help you live longer.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:35.430
My elderly neighbor says so.

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:38.110
What's the point of increasing your 
life expectancy even further?

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.540
You've already got forever.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:41.020
Want to come along?

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:42.250
No, thanks.

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:45.910
If you're staying over, please use 
the back room on the second floor.

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:47.720
I don't have another coffin, 
but there's a bed.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:48.910
Don't worry about me.

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:49.840
Okay.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:00.030
Liquor   Cigarettes

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:00.030
Bank

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:00.030
Welcome.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:08.780
Come to think of it, she's always 
been into these kinds of things.

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:14.200
I'm back.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:16.340
Ellie, do you know about convenience stores?

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:19.420
Now they even carry that makeup you like.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:23.360
Ellie?

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:33.360
<i>She always comes out of nowhere 
and then disappears again.</i>

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.870
<i>I really don't like that side of her.</i>

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:40.610
There was more I wanted to talk about.

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:46.400
Oh, well. At least it's quiet now.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:49.790
Time for bed.

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:52.000
Hi!

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.120
I've been waiting for you, Sophie!

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:59.420
I don't want you to be lonely, 
so I'll sleep next to you.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:06.310
Let's see... Where's the nearest crematorium?

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:08.590
Hey! Why are you trying to cremate me?!

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:11.430
Was there something wrong with my offer?

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:13.450
Sophie, please open up!

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:16.620
Let me out already!

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.280
Refrigerated delivery!

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:24.670
Thank you for your business!

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:31.320
The blood's finally here.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:35.320
I need to hide it so Ellie won't find it.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:37.930
She'll waste it again the moment she does.

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:41.980
Mmm, smells like blood.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.720
Where did you come from?

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.240
Good timing!

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:47.400
Let's all have dinner.

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:50.000
Sounds like a great idea!

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:52.590
I guess so.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:58.030
What's wrong?

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.510
A lot changes in a hundred years, huh?

00:14:01.510 --> 00:14:02.700
What is that?

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:07.290
A machine that uses 
electricity to wash dishes.

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:08.560
And that?

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:10.270
An induction stove.

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:14.190
It uses magnetic waves instead 
of an open flame to heat the pot.

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:16.350
Wow, that sounds convenient.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:17.680
And that's electric, too?

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:18.480
It is.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:22.460
Does that mean modern iron 
maidens are electric, as well?

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:29.980
Can they extract blood more 
efficiently than in the past?

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:34.100
There's no such thing as a modern iron maiden.

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:37.080
Oh!

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:41.020
<b>Japan's Beautiful Mountains
Top 100</b>

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:41.020
Movies have color and sound now, 
and you can watch them at home.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.250
Oh, yeah.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:45.340
You only ever saw black and white movies.

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:46.980
That brings back memories.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:51.490
There was a rumor that when a movie 
was shown for the first time,

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:54.450
the audience got scared by the train 
on the screen and ran away in panic.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:56.670
Wow, really?

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:58.090
That's so funny.

00:14:58.090 --> 00:14:59.880
It's just a projected 
picture on a flat screen.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:04.020
<i>The morning sun is so gorgeous, people 
come here just for one glimpse—</i>

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:08.360
You should research the shows 
before you watch them.

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:09.970
And what's that?

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.800
It looks like you really like it.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.420
This is a computer.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:18.670
This internet that they recently 
invented is really useful.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.440
You can look up all kinds of things, 
check up on friends who live far away,

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.830
send a letter in an instant, 
and so much more.

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:27.770
Wow, that's amazing!

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:30.020
I'll teach you how to use it.

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:35.480
You tap this, and then you 
click on the network icon.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:36.960
And to use the keyboard...

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:39.800
Ugh, this is so tedious.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:42.230
Can't you explain it more simply?

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:47.120
Jeez, I didn't even do anything 
and it started acting weird.

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:48.820
Maybe if I bang on it, it'll fix it.

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:51.890
Okay, just remember this one thing.

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:55.110
Don't ever touch my computer.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:58.300
That's easy.

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:02.520
<i>They already gave up.</i>

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:23.710
Well, I'm going to use 
the bathroom for a bit.

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:26.790
I'm going to try the makeup Sophie gave me.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:28.250
Take your time!

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:34.220
Wait... Can vampires even 
do their makeup if they can't

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.930
see themselves in the mirror?

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:47.880
Sophie?

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:50.500
Can you check to see if my makeup looks okay?

00:16:51.130 --> 00:16:53.440
I-It's... perfect.

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:57.280
That reaction...

00:16:57.280 --> 00:16:59.110
I must have messed up somewhere.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:00.820
So that's how they check it!

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:04.730
I could do your makeup, if you like.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.460
Oh, thank you.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.960
I've wanted to do this for so long!

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:21.400
There, all done!

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:23.850
Sophie, what do you think?

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:24.930
You look like usual.

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:27.660
Good! Looks like it's fine this time.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:30.060
Thank you, human girl.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:31.360
You're welcome!

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:34.700
You really are a well-trained servant.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:36.240
I'm a little jealous.

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:39.440
Akari's not a servant.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:41.040
She's not?

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.660
I assumed she was, since she lives with you.

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:48.610
That must mean you're Sophie's... um...

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:51.000
What do you think I am?

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.240
Her wife?

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.970
A live-in emergency meal or something?

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.710
No!

00:17:56.710 --> 00:17:59.050
I forgot to introduce her.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.090
Akari is my friend.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:08.220
I'm sorry, but what is 
that supposed to mean?

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:10.180
Is something wrong?

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:13.840
It's one thing to keep her around 
if she's your servant or your meal.

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:19.310
But she's a human, right? They're not like us!

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:25.420
They're monstrous beings 
that eat flesh and organs!

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:27.380
And you think you can be friends with one?

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:30.280
Says the monster who bathes in blood.

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:35.220
Vampires have always been 
feared and hated by humans.

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:37.920
The idea of befriending them is ridiculous.

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:41.370
Ellie, times have changed.

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.890
Also, Japanese people eat 
rice much more than meat.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:49.330
A long time ago, this 
is how they treated us.

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:51.180
There! It's a vampire!

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:53.190
Put a wooden stake through the heart!

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:55.150
But these days,

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:57.860
it's like this.

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:01.840
Really? This is what's come 
of the vampires' dignity?

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:06.320
But there's no telling when 
a human will betray you.

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:09.950
If you think of them as friends, you're 
sure to be hurt sooner or later.

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:15.440
Which is why it would be better 
if you and Sophie parted.

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:15.930
Huh?!

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:16.720
Hey!

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:19.760
Humans and vampires can't ever be friends.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.210
But...

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:23.480
Sophie's coming with me.

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.180
Hang on, who said you could—

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:25.980
Wait!

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:29.830
What?

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:33.610
Y-You can't just leave out of the 
blue and take her with you.

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:37.610
<i>You may be acting friendly now,</i>

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:40.610
<i>but the moment you're threatened, 
you'll show your true colors.</i>

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:42.100
<i>That's how all humans are.</i>

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:44.750
If you get in my way, I'll attack you!

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:45.700
Attack?!

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:50.650
B-Be gentle, okay?

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:53.670
Sophie, this girl's kind of scaring me!

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:56.100
Akari's always like that.

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:00.580
You really are a strange girl.

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:03.300
I am?! How?!

00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:09.730
Why aren't you afraid?

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:14.470
We're monsters with powers 
completely alien to humans.

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:18.390
But no matter what kind of 
powers you might have,

00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:21.940
I can't imagine a friend of 
Sophie-chan's doing anything bad.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:28.820
Maybe the special trait of modern people 
is to be complacent about peace?

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:32.320
Complacent about peace...

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:35.190
But maybe if it's someone as weird as you,

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:38.310
becoming friends with a vampire 
might just be possible.

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:47.080
For now, I'll accept you.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.320
Oh, I'm so glad!

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:52.440
What makes you think you're in charge?

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:54.690
Be a good friend to Sophie.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:55.410
I will!

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:59.350
And I want to get to know you better, too.

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:00.910
Thank you.

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:03.870
Well, I'll visit again soon.

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:12.750
I wonder when she'll come again.

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.110
Yeah...

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:21.630
Ellie's random, so it could be 
really soon, or decades from now.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:23.820
Decades?

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:27.960
But I could be a grandma by then!

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:38.960
<b>Episode 5</b>

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:38.960
<b>Vampire Cooking</b>

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:01.680
Is that Amason again?

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:04.380
Nice to see you, Sophie!

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:05.770
Ellie?

00:23:05.770 --> 00:23:08.640
You came again? 
That was sooner than I expected.

00:23:08.640 --> 00:23:10.490
Oh, Ellie-chan!

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:12.820
I'm here today to give you a present.

00:23:15.750 --> 00:23:16.940
This is a...

00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:18.510
A moving gift.

00:23:18.510 --> 00:23:19.500
Moving?

00:23:21.340 --> 00:23:23.720
I moved into this neighborhood,

00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:26.470
so now I can easily come visit you anytime!

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:31.850
I'm going to go buy 100 crucifixes 
to set up around my house.

00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:35.420
But then you won't be able 
to get in or out, either.

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:38.300
I look forward to hanging out together!
